# PRD §7.4 makes byte-identical layout across machines a hard requirement, and
# PRD §16 runs the golden-file layout test on two operating systems. A CRLF
# checkout on Windows would change every hash derived from a file's bytes and
# make that test fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the layout engine.
* text eol=lf

# Transcript fixtures are compared byte-for-byte by the parser tests.
*.jsonl -text
*.png binary
*.wgsl text eol=lf
